WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.390
- Since it's design week,

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.530
we wanted to put our
design skills to the test

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:06.840
in a little something we're
calling "Design Derby".

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.754
- Yeah!
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.754 --> 00:00:11.640
- But gosh, I would
love a worthy adversary

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.370
who's as design obsessed as me. (gasps)

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.410
I'm so lucky.
(Ross laughing)

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.670
I know of someone.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:19.080
It is comedian, actor, author,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.410
woman extraordinaire, host
of "The Circle" on Netflix,

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.342
and design darling and our
dear friend, Michelle Buteau!

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:28.076
- Oh, my gosh!
(audience cheering)

00:00:28.076 --> 00:00:30.986
Oh, my gosh, it's me!
(Ross laughing)

00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:34.150
- And, of course, we have the best host

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.450
to take us through it all,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.050
it's Rossi Ross Matthews.
- That's right!

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.330
This is a very serious game,

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.900
and here's how it's gonna go down, ladies.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.480
I'm gonna ask you a series
of design related questions.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.260
You'll each write your answer

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.093
on your little

00:00:48.093 --> 00:00:49.290
whiteboard right there.
- Okay. Okay.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.880
- And whoever gets the most right

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.778
wins a prize for their
half of the audience.

00:00:53.778 --> 00:00:54.690
- Ooh.
- Hey!

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.723
- Whoa!
- Which half am I?

00:00:55.723 --> 00:00:57.180
Which half is Michelle?

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.013
- All right, Drew.

00:00:58.013 --> 00:00:59.130
You're playing for that
half of the audience

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.196
over there.
- Hi, guys!

00:01:00.196 --> 00:01:02.157
(audience cheering)

00:01:02.157 --> 00:01:03.481
- And Michelle, this is your half

00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:04.314
of the audience right here.

00:01:04.314 --> 00:01:05.578
You're playing for them!

00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:07.623
- Give it up! Give it up!

00:01:07.623 --> 00:01:09.332
(audience cheering)

00:01:09.332 --> 00:01:11.900
- Okay.
- What are we winning?

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.280
I'm so excited.
- I'll tell you

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.687
at the end.
- Okay.

00:01:14.687 --> 00:01:16.088
- Oh, god, there's stakes.

00:01:16.088 --> 00:01:17.450
- There are stakes.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.490
All right, let's go.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.000
Question number one. Take a look at this.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.330
This is an Arco floor lamp.
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.960
- It became popular when it appeared

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.450
in the 1971 Sean Connery
film, "Diamonds Are Forever".

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.040
It has a very heavy, marble base.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.480
How much does this lamp cost?

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.710
- Oh!
- Write it down on your board.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.360
Whoever gets closest without
going over gets the point.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.640
Like "Price Is Right" style.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.110
Michelle, why don't you-
- Why am I nervous?

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.470
- Why don't you reveal-
- Because you have

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.983
a whole group of people
- I know,

00:01:44.983 --> 00:01:46.040
you're counting on me.
- You're playing for.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.820
- I don't wanna let you down.
(audience cheering)

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.730
- All right.
- Okay.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.563
- Let's take a look

00:01:50.563 --> 00:01:52.870
at how much you think
that Arco floor lamp is.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.750
- I mean, it depends
where you get it from,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.460
but I'm gonna say around here.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.270
- 3,200 to 3,300, okay.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.730
All right. Good guess.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.550
Drew, 2,500.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:08.457
Okay the actual price for
that Arco lamp is $3,695.

00:02:10.351 --> 00:02:11.184
- Oh!
- Michelle!

00:02:11.184 --> 00:02:13.401
- Oh, I got it!
- Yeah!

00:02:13.401 --> 00:02:15.300
- [Michelle] Oh, my goodness!

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.060
- Michelle got that right,

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.330
which means this side of the audience,

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.552
you have one point.
- Whoo!

00:02:19.552 --> 00:02:21.348
- Drew's still trying to catch up.

00:02:21.348 --> 00:02:22.696
(audience cheering)

00:02:22.696 --> 00:02:25.230
- [Michelle] We did
it. I'm so proud of us.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.810
- All right, question number
two is a drawing challenge.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.820
- Oh.
- Oh, no.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:31.710
- Yeah, you're gonna draw.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:36.680
You have 20 seconds to draw
the famous Eames Lounge Chair.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.280
This is an iconic chair
that popped up in TV shows

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.520
like "Frasier", "House",

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.898
and every gay in Palm Springs has it.

00:02:43.898 --> 00:02:45.269
(Ross chuckling)
(audience laughing)

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:46.570
- With the, I'm not,

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.340
I didn't go to art school.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.037
- Who's got the best version?
- This is not good.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.693
A drawing challenge?
- Okay.

00:02:52.693 --> 00:02:54.610
And time is up. Time is up.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.505
Reveal. Drew, reveal yours.

00:02:56.505 --> 00:02:58.857
Well done, actually.

00:02:58.857 --> 00:03:00.860
Michelle, let's take a look at yours.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.876
- I mean, you know.

00:03:02.876 --> 00:03:07.400
(Michelle laughing)
(audience applauding)

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.630
- Well, let's see how close they got.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.343
This is what the actual
Eames chair looks like.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.210
- Yes.
- Okay.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.720
So you know what?

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.550
I actually think you both get a point,

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.082
because you both did really well.

00:03:21.082 --> 00:03:22.479
- Oh, okay, Oprah.

00:03:22.479 --> 00:03:24.690
You get a point, you get a point.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.485
- Okay.
- My team is mad.

00:03:26.485 --> 00:03:27.990
My team is mad.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.767
I see hands up there not liking it.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.340
- Oh, yeah.
- Shots fired.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:32.300
- All right.
- Pew, pew, pew.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.851
- Listen, everyone calm down.

00:03:33.851 --> 00:03:36.760
The game is two for
Michelle, one for Drew,

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.250
but anyone can still win this.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.083
Let's go to question

00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:40.020
number three.
- All right. Oh, gosh.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.247
- All right, a hugely popular

00:03:41.247 --> 00:03:43.490
furniture and design store

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.060
